VirtIO GPU transport for vmx

Wire layouts follow VirtIO 1.2, sections 4.1 (PCI) and 5.7 (GPU):
https://docs.oasis-open.org/virtio/virtio/v1.2/virtio-v1.2.html

GPU definitions: include/uapi/linux/virtio_gpu.h from Linux v6.12,
revision adc218676eef25575469234709c2d87185ca223a.
Copyright Red Hat, Inc. 2013-2014; Dave Airlie and Gerd Hoffmann.
The BSD notice is preserved in LICENSE.gpu.

VirGL command layouts: src/virgl_protocol.h and src/virgl_hw.h from
virglrenderer revision 4d8bd3c9954a9599e0de70a2e432c761da80398d.
Copyright 2014, 2015 Red Hat. The MIT notice is in LICENSE.gpu.
Retrieved from the Chromium mirror:
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/virglrenderer/+/4d8bd3c9954a9599e0de70a2e432c761da80398d/

The native implementation reuses vmx's PCI, split virtqueues, window and
input code. It exposes VirtIO GPU capability set 1 through the generated9
gpu(3) file interface, remapping resource identifiers while preserving
guest context and object namespaces. No Mesa or virglrenderer code is
linked into vmx. New integration code uses the generated9 root LICENSE;
existing vmx code retains its original authorship and license.
